{"name":"Aragon","hex":"#b06455","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Aragon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An autonomous community in northeastern Spain. Capital: Zaragoza.","A river in the autonomous communities of Aragon and Navarre, Spain; in full, Aragon River."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Aragon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aragon","blocks":[{"text":"Aragon is an autonomous community in Spain, coextensive with the medieval Kingdom of Aragon. In northeastern Spain, the Aragonese autonomous community comprises three provinces : Huesca, Zaragoza, and Teruel. Its capital is Zaragoza. The current Statute of Autonomy declares Aragon a historic nationality of Spain."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flag_of_Aragon.svg/330px-Flag_of_Aragon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aragon","wikidata":"Q4040"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ermita_de_la_Virgen_de_la_Pe%C3%B1a%2C_LIC_Sierras_de_Santo_Domingo_y_Caballera%2C_Ani%C3%A9s%2C_Huesca%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-06%2C_DD_08-09_PAN.JPG/500px-Ermita_de_la_Virgen_de_la_Pe%C3%B1a%2C_LIC_Sierras_de_Santo_Domingo_y_Caballera%2C_Ani%C3%A9s%2C_Huesca%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-06%2C_DD_08-09_PAN.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ermita_de_la_Virgen_de_la_Pe%C3%B1a%2C_LIC_Sierras_de_Santo_Domingo_y_Caballera%2C_Ani%C3%A9s%2C_Huesca%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-06%2C_DD_08-09_PAN.JPG/1280px-Ermita_de_la_Virgen_de_la_Pe%C3%B1a%2C_LIC_Sierras_de_Santo_Domingo_y_Caballera%2C_Ani%C3%A9s%2C_Huesca%2C_Espa%C3%B1a%2C_2015-01-06%2C_DD_08-09_PAN.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/da/Ermita_de_la_Virgen_de_la_Pe%C3%B1a%2C_LIC_